      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink id="cda9-f5bd-31d8-9029" name="Ork Vehicle Upgrades" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="7ab0-3a69-56f8-540b" type="selectionEntryGroup">
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry id="a0c9-eced-84c2-4afb" name="Red Paint Job" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="9c7c-badb-34f2-5673" type="max"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule id="eb54-fd88-f19d-4ed1" name="Red Paint Job" hidden="false">
                  <description>Ork vehicles with red paint jobs add +1 to their move in the Movement phase but do not incur penalties for this extra inch. For example, a vehicle could move 13&quot; and still count as moving 12&quot;.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry id="4908-6b16-604b-4c70" name="Searchlight" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="e418-8cc9-aab1-9c16" type="max"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule id="8314-4c0d-c8d0-34e5" name="Searchlight" hidden="false">
                  <description>Searchlights are only used in missions where the rules for night fighting are being used. They allow one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle or Dreadnought to be fired at by all other Ork units that are in range and have a line of fire. However, the vehicle or Dreadnought using the Searchlight in this manner is considered visible to all enemy units who have line of sight on the next turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="1.0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry id="6da6-ee40-134e-6d3c" name="Stikkabomb Chucka" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="8734-480e-9de7-be12" type="max"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule id="6456-1edd-f360-acc6" name="Stikkabomb Chucka" hidden="false">
                  <description>Any walker, or unit disembarking from a vehicle, with a stikkbomb chukka is treated as having stikkbombs if they charge into combat.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry id="8782-ddfe-576c-f648" name="Bigbomm" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="2.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="58f6-dd8e-a629-2dc6" type="max"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule id="59e1-956a-5dc9-d97c" name="Bigbomm" hidden="false">
                  <description>Once per game per upgrade taken, a Warkopta with a Bigbomm may make a special attack, even if it has moved flat out that turn. Place the large blast template with the central hole on  a model that the Warkopta has passed over during its movement phase. The Bigbomm scatters D6&quot; and is resolved with Strength 4 and AP5.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="15.0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
